# Environment for antimage-panel, e.g. /etc/antimage/panel.env loaded with
# EnvironmentFile= in the systemd unit.
#
# The panel is configured by FLAGS, not by a config file. This file exists only
# for the two environment variables it honours.

# ANTIMAGE_MASTER_KEY  (base64 of 32 raw bytes, optional)
#   Supplies the master key instead of <data-dir>/master.key. It encrypts TOTP
#   secrets and the CA private key, so a leaked database without it yields
#   neither.
#
#   Generate with:  head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64
#
#   SECURITY: prefer the 0600 file on disk unless your platform injects secrets
#   by environment. An environment variable is visible to anything that can read
#   /proc/<pid>/environ and is easy to leak into logs and crash reports.
#   LOSING THIS VALUE IS UNRECOVERABLE: the CA key and every TOTP secret go with
#   it. Back it up separately from the database.
# ANTIMAGE_MASTER_KEY=

# ANTIMAGE_DEV_PROXY  (URL, optional)
#   Proxies UI requests to a Vite dev server instead of serving the embedded
#   build.
#   SECURITY: DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Never set this in production -- it makes the
#   panel serve whatever that origin returns.
# ANTIMAGE_DEV_PROXY=http://localhost:5173
